The issue is that `NullableTypeDeclarationFixer` is incorrectly inserting a space before the type declaration when it should preserve existing whitespace (specifically newlines in multi-line parameter lists).

In the original code:
```php
if (!$tokens[$typeAnalysis->getStartIndex() - 1]->equals('(')) {
    $tokens->ensureWhitespaceAtIndex($typeAnalysis->getStartIndex() - 1, 1, ' ');
}
```
The fixer checks if the token immediately preceding the type is an opening parenthesis. If it is not, it forces a single space (`' '`). In the multi-line case, the token preceding the type is a whitespace token containing a newline and indentation. Since this whitespace token is not `(`, the fixer replaces the newline/indentation with a single space, effectively "eating" the newline and pulling the parameter up to the function declaration line.

The patch changes the condition to:
```php
if (!$tokens[$typeAnalysis->getStartIndex() - 1]->equals('(') && !$tokens[$typeAnalysis->getStartIndex() - 1]->isWhitespace()) {
    $tokens->ensureWhitespaceAtIndex($typeAnalysis->getStartIndex() - 1, 1, ' ');
}
```
By adding `&& !$tokens[...]->isWhitespace()`, the fixer will no longer force a space if there is already whitespace (like a newline) present. This preserves the multi-line formatting while still ensuring a space is added when the type immediately follows a non-parenthesis token without spacing.

This directly addresses the reported bug and maintains existing behavior for single-line declarations.

